# ── Chapter 2 fidelity pins: "Standing, and Why It Is Never Revoked" ─────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   nibli-pin --kb new-book-plans/utopia-v2.nibli book-1/02-standing.pins.nibli
#
# One entry per load-bearing sentence. Private to the author.

:expect-pins 12

# "The court has standing... They have it by being what they are."
? public(Court).
# => TRUE

? authority(Court).
# => TRUE

# "The second is that the electorate seats you."
? choose(Electorate, Boss).
# => TRUE

? authority(Boss).
# => TRUE

# "no route that runs through your own hands" — standing cannot be self-conferred
:refuse reasoning /declared derived-only/
authority(Pax).

# "Someone with a great deal of power and no standing cannot write themselves in."
# Ivo was never seated and is not a public body.
? authority(Ivo).
# => FALSE

# "Then the electorate recalled Boss." / "Boss holds no credential"
? broken(Boss).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, Boss).
# => FALSE

# "But Boss still has standing. Permanently." — the chapter's whole argument.
# authority(Boss) above is TRUE *despite* broken(Boss) being TRUE.

# "Rebel exposed Boss." / "Rebel is shielded because Boss is an authority."
? show(Rebel, Boss).
# => TRUE

? defend(Rebel).
# => TRUE

# "Rebel is not imprisoned, and the case against Rebel does not proceed."
? prisoner(Rebel).
# => FALSE

? false(Rebel).
# => FALSE
